NAME
    trace - arm a live CPU instruction trace

SYNOPSIS
    trace <count>
    trace off

DESCRIPTION
    Arms the attached core's live CPU instruction trace for the next
    <count> instructions starting immediately (rather than from power-on),
    or cancels an active trace early with 'trace off'.

    <count> is parsed as hexadecimal (optional '0x' or '$' prefix) and
    must be at least 1 (for example, 'trace 100' traces 0x100 = 256
    instructions, and 'trace 500' traces 0x500 = 1,280 instructions).
    Cores without a live trace hook print a message indicating no trace
    switch is registered.

OPTIONS
    <count>
        Hexadecimal number of instructions to trace (>= 1).

    off
        Cancel any in-progress instruction trace.

EXAMPLES
    trace 100
    trace 0x500
    trace off

EXIT STATUS
    0   Trace armed or disabled (or usage/unavailable message printed).
    1   Count less than 1, invalid hex value, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    log(1), step(1), disasm(1), bp(1), cov(1)
